 ## Background
-Iterative Bisection Intersection Refinement is a technique used in real-time volume graphics and isosurface rendering. It was described in the context of real-time ray-casting and advanced shading of discrete isosurfaces by Sigg et al. in 2005 [S2]. The method is also referenced in the book "Real-Time Volume Graphics" by Hadwiger et al. [S1]. It is used in volume rendering pipelines, such as the VTK `vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper2` [S3]. The technique is particularly useful for improving the visual quality of isosurface rendering without significantly impacting performance [G].
